{# WHICH PROPERTY NAMES THE ZONES — the one thing about a file the person may
   know better than the reader does. A file with both `Name` and `layer` in it
   has two plausible answers; left blank, the first spelling that names EVERY
   feature is used and the summary says which it was.

   IT IS READ ONCE AND DISCARDED with the rest of the file: what survives is the
   property's name in the provenance row, not a setting the area now carries. #}
<div class="zfrow">
    <label class="fldlab" for="nameprop">Names from</label>
    <select class="fld" id="nameprop" name="nameProperty">
        <option value="">the first that names every feature</option>
        {% for property in nameProperties %}<option value="{{ property }}">{{ property }}</option>{% endfor %}
    </select>
    <span class="zfnote">read once, then discarded</span>
</div>
